// Xunara Platform API v2 over gRPC (M8d, M8e).
//
// PlatformService mirrors the read-mostly /api/v2 surface of one organization
// so automation can use a typed protocol instead of scraping JSON. It is part
// of the platform plane: it never touches the Tailscale compatibility core
// (TS2021, Noise, MapRequest), and credentials are the same service API keys
// the HTTP API accepts.
//
// PlatformAdminService mirrors /api/platform/v1, the deployment-level surface
// a multi-tenant operator automates. It accepts only the process-level
// platform admin token.
//
// In a multi-tenant deployment the organization for PlatformService is chosen
// by the gRPC authority (":authority"), the HTTP/2 equivalent of the Host
// header, so one listener serves every organization exactly like the HTTP
// router does. PlatformAdminService is deployment-scoped and ignores the
// authority.

